# Introduction  

We're using the {targets}^[{targets} user manual ([books.ropensci.org/targets/targets.html](https://books.ropensci.org/targets/targets.html))] R package to help manage our whole machine learning (ML) pipeline, but it is particularly helpful for the initial ETL noted on this page.   


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
# Packages
library(tidyverse)
library(here)
library(targets)
library(gt)
library(gtExtras)
library(sf)
library(leaflet)
library(osdatahub)
library(readxl)

# Sources all R/*.R same as _targets.R
tar_source()       

# ggplot theme
set_theme(theme_minimal())
```
:::


# Source    


::: {#tbl-ingest .cell .column-page-right tbl-cap='Data ingested (via `_targets.R` & `R\ingest.R`)'}

```{.r .cell-code}
path_transport_data_xls <- here("resources","sheffield_transport_datasets.xlsx")

# Read a list of our raw datasets from a spreadsheet
df_ingested <- read_xlsx(
  path_transport_data_xls, 
  sheet = "Raw datasets", 
  skip = 3
)

# List the raw datasets ingested
df_ingested |>
  mutate(Row = row_number(), .before = 1) |>
  my_gt() |>
  fmt(
      columns = "Row",
      fns = function(x) {format(round(x, 0), nsmall = 0, big.mark = ",")}
    ) |>
  cols_label(Row = "") |>
  opt_css("
    td:nth-child(6) {
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
      word-break: break-word;
    }
  ")
```

